      "origin": "Sol",
      "passive_list": {
        "0": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p>When you rest inside or near a settlement, you may choose one option: you learn what the locals are mainly angry about or afraid of, or you create a contact that lives and operates in this area – give them a name and specialization, and the Game Master tells you what they ask of you (they might request a payment or need help).</p>",
          "passive_name": "AGITATOR",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "quirk"
        },
        "1": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Requirements: you must have Skill Level 2 or higher in Dodge (see Rogue), and must have a Dexterity base die size of d10 or higher.</span></span></p><p>As long as you have <strong>no shields</strong> and no <strong>martial armor</strong> equipped, you gain the following benefits:</p><p>- You may use the <strong>Protect Skill</strong> (see Guardian) even if you have not acquired it.</p><p>- You treat your Skill Level in Dodge as being increased by 2 (to a maximum of 5).</p><p>- When you use the <strong>Protect Skill</strong> during another creature's turn, damage you suffer is reduced by an amount equal to【your current Dexterity die size】 until the end of that turn (before applying Affinities).</p>",
          "passive_name": "AGILE DEFENDER STYLE",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "heroic_style"
        },
        "2": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Requirements: you must have mastered one or more Classes among Rogue and Weaponmaster.</span></span></p><p>While you have one or more <strong>melee dagger</strong> weapons equipped, you gain a <strong>+1 bonus to Defense and Magic Defense</strong>, and you treat those weapons as also belonging to the <strong>brawling, sword, and thrown</strong> Categories for the purpose of Skills and effects.</p><p>Additionally, your attacks with weapons that belong to the dagger Category may target creatures that cannot normally be targeted by melee attacks.</p>",
          "passive_name": "BLADE ADEPT",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "heroic_skill"
        },
        "3": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Requirements: you must have mastered one or more Classes among Dancer and Weaponmaster.</span></span></p><p>As long as you have a <strong>one-handed melee weapon</strong> that belongs to the <strong>dagger or sword </strong>Categories equipped in each of your normal hand slots, you may treat your armor slot as if it were a second off-hand slot. You may only use this special slot to equip a onehanded melee weapon that belongs to the dagger or sword Categories</p><p>When you perform the <strong>Attack action</strong> while you have <strong>three daggers and/or swords </strong>equipped, you may attack once with each weapon. This follows the normal rules for two-weapon fighting: each of the three attacks loses the multi property and cannot gain it, and you treat the High Roll (HR) of each Accuracy Check as being equal to 0 when determining damage.</p>",
          "passive_name": "TRIPLE SLASH",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "heroic_skill"
        },
        "4": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Once before the next rest, after the target performs a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Group Check </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">as </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">leader </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">or performs a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Check to examine someone or something</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">, they may add a bonus of +4 to the Result of that Check</span> <br style=\" font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: -webkit-auto; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; \"></p>",
          "passive_name": "Planning",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp activity"
        },
        "5": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Once before the next rest, if the target is about to recover Mind Points, they may </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">double </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">the amount of Mind Points recovered.</span> <br style=\" font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: -webkit-auto; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; \"></p>",
          "passive_name": "Pep Talk",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp activity"
        }
      },
